        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Trump sacks attorney general Bondi, Hegseth asks US Army Chief of Staff to step down Americas Issued on: 02/04/2026 - 22:26 Modified: 02/04/2026 - 22:56 US President Donald Trump fired Attorney General Pam Bondi on Thursday after months of strained relations and named his former personal lawyer to serve as the acting chief of the Justice Department. Pentagon ​chief ​Pete Hegseth has asked the ​U.S. ‌Army ⁠Chief ‌of Staff ⁠Randy George to step ​down ‌and take immediate ‌retirement. The Guardian Washington DC bureau chief David Smith reports. 'He wasn't convincing to the world and to the American people', former US ambassador to NATO says 02/04/2026 Americas 'Gravest crime against humanity: Brazil still suffers from effects of slavery' 01/04/2026 Americas US Supreme Court rules against ban on 'conversion therapy' for LGBTQ minors 31/03/2026 Americas 'The hypocrisy was so stark' expert says, as US reverses course on Cuba oil blockade 30/03/2026 Americas Russian oil arrives in Cuba following Trump turnaround on Cuban blockade 30/03/2026 Americas Cuba to receive shipment of Russia oil after US lifts pressure 30/03/2026 Americas Russian oil tanker nears Cuba, Trump softens de facto blockade rhetoric 30/03/2026 Americas Massive protests against Trump across US 29/03/2026 Americas 'No Kings' rallies draw crowds across US 29/03/2026 Americas"
